RUN 4: at min arm len at 5 and min len at 10. 
Rule 1 — Core overlap (≥1 nt)
  Each arm fragment must touch at least 1 nucleotide of the core arm.
  Ensures the read genuinely comes from this stem interaction.

Rule 2 — Junction constraint (MAX_JUNCTION_UNPAIRED = 2)
  The ligation-facing end of each fragment can go at most 2 nt
  past the core boundary toward the other arm.
  Biologically: allows 0–2 unpaired bases at the chimeric junction,
  matching what real DDD reads show.

Rule 3 — No within-read arm overlap (checked in make_one_read)
  first_frag.overlaps(second_frag) → rejected.
  The two arm fragments of one read must never overlap in sequence space.

